<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">State of Kuwait</h1><p class="st-meta">1961 CE – present · capital Kuwait City</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Independent Kuwait since 1961, an oil-rich emirate with an elected parliament that survived Iraqi invasion and occupation in 1990-1991.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>On 19 June 1961 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> ended the 1899 protection agreement and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-kuwait">Sheikhdom of Kuwait</a> became fully independent under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdullah-al-salim-al-sabah">Abdullah Al-Salim Al-Sabah</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq's</a> ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-karim-qasim">Abd al-Karim Qasim</a> immediately claimed Kuwait, and British and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arab-league">Arab League</a> troops deployed to deter an invasion.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A constitution of 1962 created the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-assembly-of-kuwait">National Assembly</a>, the most powerful elected parliament in the Gulf, though the emir retains wide powers and has suspended it several times. Oil revenues financed a welfare state, free education and health care, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-kuwait">Kuwait</a> Fund for Arab development aid. Kuwaiti citizens are a minority among a large foreign workforce.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> invaded on 2 August 1990 and occupied <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-kuwait">Kuwait</a> until a US-led coalition liberated it in February 1991. Kuwait rebuilt and remains a constitutional <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-sabah">Al Sabah</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/state-of-kuwait.jpg" alt="State of Kuwait" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Wikimedia Commons · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Kuwait.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1961 CE – present</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kuwait City</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abdullah Al-Salim Al-Sabah, Jaber Al-Ahmad Al-Sabah, Sabah Al-Ahmad Al-Jaber Al-Sabah</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Islam (Sunni majority, Shi'a minority)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Kuwait</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kuwait</dd></dl></aside></div>
